{
  "id": 473994852,
  "iid": 24378,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "CMake: Follow the rules on generating files for multiple targets",
  "description": "Per the CMake documentation[1]:\n\n        Do not list the output in more than one independent target that\n        may build in parallel or the instances of the rule may conflict.\n        Instead, use the add_custom_target() command to drive the command\n        and make the other targets depend on that one. See the Example:\n        Generating Files for Multiple Targets below.\n\nWhere that example says roughly the same thing and describes possible race\nconditions. The most obvious consequence of this is the Xcode \"new build\nsystem\" complaining and refusing to generate.\n\nFollow the example and create targets for the output code that the other\ntargets that use the output file both depend on. If they both depended\non the compiled code, we could use an object library, but many (most?)\nof these issues have to do with checkAPI, which uses the source.\n\nIf the autogen target is doing to depend on the translation qm files,\nit needs to also depend on the target that includes the qm files, so\nthat CMake (and the XCode generator in particular), is satisfied that\nit can determine what order to process the targets.\n\nPing #18885.\n\nThere are still issues around multiple commands creating the same\ndirectory, which is also a no-no for XCode.\n\n1 - https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/command/add_custom_command.html\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
